                                    <h1>D2C Payment Gateway Selection Guide 2026-2027</h1>
                                    <p>Payment gateway is critical D2C infrastructure decision — affects conversion + transaction cost + fraud + international expansion + operational reliability. India (Razorpay + Cashfree + PayU + CCAvenue + PhonePe) + international (Stripe + PayPal + Adyen + Braintree) + regional (regional payment methods). Different fees + features + regional strengths. Here is the complete D2C payment gateway selection guide.</p>
                                    <h2>India Payment Gateway Landscape</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Razorpay:</strong> Peak India D2C payment gateway — strong Shopify + startup + D2C ecosystem + comprehensive features + Razorpay Route (marketplace) + subscription.<br><strong>Cashfree:</strong> Strong D2C + emerging + comprehensive features + payouts + international.<br><strong>PayU India:</strong> Established + PayU LazyPay (BNPL) + comprehensive features.<br><strong>CCAvenue:</strong> Legacy + established + international payment strong.<br><strong>PhonePe / Google Pay Business:</strong> UPI + wallet-primary + growing merchant.<br><strong>Paytm Payment Gateway:</strong> Paytm ecosystem integrated.<br><strong>Direct UPI + wallet:</strong> UPI + wallet direct integration for large merchants.</p>
                                    <h2>India Payment Fees + Economics</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Domestic transaction fees:</strong> 1.5-2.5% typical + GST 18% on fees.<br><strong>UPI + specific method fees:</strong> Different fees for different methods (UPI cheaper than cards).<br><strong>International transaction fees:</strong> 3-4.5%+ for international cards.<br><strong>Setup + integration fees:</strong> Often zero setup + integration + tech-development cost.<br><strong>Recurring + subscription fees:</strong> Additional 0.5-1% for recurring subscription setup.<br><strong>Chargeback + dispute fees:</strong> Per-dispute fees + operational cost.<br><strong>Payout + settlement timing:</strong> T+1 to T+3 typical settlement + faster payout options.<br><strong>Volume-based tiered pricing:</strong> Volume-based tiered pricing negotiable at scale.</p>
                                    <h2>International Payment Gateway Landscape</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Stripe:</strong> Global + developer-friendly + comprehensive features + strong USA + Europe + expanding globally.<br><strong>PayPal + Braintree:</strong> Established + wide consumer trust + PayPal payments + Braintree gateway.<br><strong>Adyen:</strong> Enterprise + omnichannel + international + Europe origin.<br><strong>Klarna:</strong> BNPL + Europe origin + growing USA.<br><strong>Affirm:</strong> USA BNPL + credit + growing.<br><strong>Regional gateways:</strong><br>- Alipay + WeChat Pay (China).<br>- iDEAL (Netherlands) + Bancontact (Belgium) + Sofort (Germany).<br>- Mercado Pago (Latin America).<br>- MPesa (Africa).<br>- Regional-specific payment methods essential for market entry.</p>
                                    <h2>International Payment Fees + Economics</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Stripe / PayPal fees USA + international:</strong> 2.9% + $0.30 typical + additional international + currency conversion.<br><strong>European transaction fees:</strong> Lower European card fees.<br><strong>International currency conversion:</strong> 1-3% additional on top of transaction fees.<br><strong>Chargeback + dispute fees:</strong> $15-25 per dispute.<br><strong>Compliance + regulatory fees:</strong> KYC + compliance + PCI DSS + regulatory setup.<br><strong>Enterprise pricing:</strong> Custom enterprise pricing at scale — negotiable.<br><strong>Payout timing:</strong> Different by region — USA T+2 typical + international varies.</p>
                                    <h2>Multi-Gateway Strategy</h2>
                                    <p>Scaling D2C brands often multi-gateway:<br><strong>Primary gateway per region:</strong> Razorpay India + Stripe international + regional gateway per major market.<br><strong>Failover + redundancy:</strong> Secondary gateway for failover + downtime protection.<br><strong>Method optimisation:</strong> Different methods routed to optimal gateway (UPI to Razorpay + cards to another).<br><strong>Regional payment method coverage:</strong> Regional payment methods essential (UPI + Alipay + MPesa + regional).<br><strong>BNPL + specific product coverage:</strong> BNPL + specific product coverage per gateway.<br><strong>Ops complexity + reporting:</strong> Multi-gateway ops complexity + reporting + reconciliation.<br>Multi-gateway at scale + growth stage. Single gateway for early stage simplicity.</p>
                                    <h2>Payment Gateway Selection Framework</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Business stage + volume:</strong> Early stage — single gateway simplicity. Growth stage — multi-gateway optimisation.<br><strong>Regional focus:</strong> Primary regional focus determines primary gateway.<br><strong>Payment method priorities:</strong> UPI-heavy India + card-heavy international + regional-specific methods.<br><strong>Recurring + subscription needs:</strong> Subscription-focused D2C needs strong recurring capability.<br><strong>Fraud + chargeback risk:</strong> High-fraud categories need strong fraud + chargeback tools.<br><strong>Engineering capability:</strong> Developer-friendly gateways (Stripe + Razorpay) require + reward engineering.<br><strong>Support + operational needs:</strong> Regional support + operational needs.<br><strong>Integration + ecosystem:</strong> Shopify + Magento + platform integration.</p>
                                    <h2>Common Payment Gateway Mistakes</h2>
                                    <p>1. <strong>Single-gateway lock-in at scale:</strong> Single gateway creates single-point failure + no redundancy at scale.<br>2. <strong>Under-investment in fraud + chargeback tools:</strong> Fraud + chargebacks destroy unit economics.<br>3. <strong>Missing regional payment methods:</strong> Regional-specific payment methods essential for regional market entry.<br>4. <strong>Poor payment method routing:</strong> Different methods should route to optimal gateway.<br>5. <strong>Ignoring settlement + payout timing:</strong> Settlement + payout timing affects working capital.<br>6. <strong>No recurring + subscription strategy:</strong> Missing recurring + subscription capability for consumable D2C.<br>7. <strong>Over-complex early stage:</strong> Over-complex payment stack early stage before revenue justifies complexity.</p>

